<h1>1.0 Document Purpose</h1>
<p>
The main purpose of this Software Requirement Specification (SRS) document is to provide a complete description about the functional and non-functional requirements for the project titled “Plumbfix: Plumbing Management System.” This project will be focused on improving the plumbing repair service operations for customers, plumbers, and business administrators through a web-based platform that includes online booking scheduling, deposit payment verification, automated refund calculations, plumber job completion logging, real-time live chat, and seasonal demand analytics.
</p>
<p>
The actual idea to develop this system is originated from the issues found in the current plumbing service management process, where the booking and service delivery experience for customers is often limited to unorganized phone calls, lost paper notes, and verbal confirmations. Many customers struggle to track technician availability, verify online deposit payments, and get transparent receipts. Homeowners and even plumbing service business managers also face challenges in manually dispatching plumbers, calculating complex cancellation refunds, and managing sudden surges in repair demands during heavy monsoonal rain seasons.
</p>
<p>
Therefore, this system is designated to address these challenges by transforming traditional manual methods into a more efficient and automated digital platform. The main objective of this system is to support the end-to-end plumbing service journey with features, interfaces, and capabilities of the system by providing a foundation for the design and development process.
</p>

<h1>1.1 Product Scope</h1>
<p>
The scope of this system is to provide customers, plumbers, and administrators with a reliable, transparent, and interactive platform to manage plumbing repair services seamlessly. The system will include the main functions such as interactive booking scheduling which customers can select repair categories, dates, and available time slots from an interactive calendar view in a convenient way. Next, is the deposit payment and slip verification which the customers will be provided with deposit upload options for a fixed RM 70.00 deposit while administrators review slips, trigger automated PDF invoice generation, and assign plumbers to confirmed bookings. This system will also cover automated cancellation and refund engine which calculates refund eligibility based on 24-hour and 48-hour notice policies, logs pending refund records, and facilitates administrator bank transfer proof uploads. Other than that, a plumber job completion sheet logging will be presented with labor charges, material costs, work notes, and completion photos to help record service completion. A real-time live chat communication and push notification system will guide the customers and plumbers to communicate effectively during active bookings and also will allow monitoring of service statuses.
</p>
<p>
The platform will be web-based, making it accessible across devices such as PC, laptops, tablets, and smartphones without installation needed. The subsystems of the system also will be included which are the customer subsystem, the staff and plumber subsystem, and the admin subsystem.
</p>
<p>
The expected benefits are to encourage customers to engage with plumbing service scheduling in a reliable, fast, and transparent way. Also, to support the administrators and plumbers in managing service dispatching using an interactive platform. Other than that, it can also provide admins with the ability to verify deposit payments, approve refunds, and view seasonal analytics easily.
</p>

<h1>1.2 Intended Audience and Document Overview</h1>
<p>
This document is intended to the readers that involved in the development of Plumbfix: Plumbing Management System, including stakeholder, developer, project manager and documentation writers. Developers will use this document to understand the detailed functional and non-functional requirements that guide the system’s design, coding, and integration of modules, such as real-time chat, deposit verification, and PDF invoice generation. Project manager will refer this document to plan, schedule, and monitor the overall development process to make sure that the project meets the defined scope, objectives, and timeline. Stakeholders which is the users can also refer to this SRS in order to understand the system’s purpose, benefits, and features that support automated plumbing service management in a user-friendly environment. Documentation writers will depend on this SRS document to ensure that all user manuals and help guide accurately in describing the system’s usage and navigation.
</p>
<p>
Furthermore, this document is organized into several main sections such as Section 1, which introduces the document’s purpose, scope, and intended audience. Section 2 provides an overall description of the product, its users, and constraints. Section 3 outlines the system’s functional requirements while Section 4 outlines the non-functional requirements such as usability, reliability, and security and lastly Section 5 which describes the system interfaces and the design constraints. Note that readers are advised to start with the overview in Section 1 to gain the gist of the project, followed by Section 2 for a general understanding, while developers should really focus more on Sections 3 and 4, and project managers on Sections 1 and 2. Documentation writers may refer to all sections, particularly Sections 3 and 5 for accurate system details and structure.
</p>

